1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:41,250
Ah! I slept too long!

2
00:01:48,570 --> 00:01:51,990
I don't hear anything. There's no heartbeat.

3
00:01:52,710 --> 00:01:54,510
It's because you're listening through his armor.

4
00:01:55,790 --> 00:01:58,210
Looks like he finally managed to fall asleep.

5
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:02,570
Suppose that means his food poisoning settled down.

6
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:05,810
Oh, Laios, what a troublemaker.

7
00:02:06,550 --> 00:02:08,110
Let's let him sleep a bit longer.

8
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:10,750
He was tossing and turning off through the night.

9
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:13,550
I wonder about this dungeon.

10
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:17,810
Does it already know how many monsters need to be defeated on each floor?

11
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:21,810
Killing monsters in here just stabilizes the ecosystem.

12
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:26,230
But if we don't do it, the village will get completely overrun by them.

13
00:02:26,230 --> 00:02:30,670
And when the village does get overwhelmed, it recruits adventurers to help.

14
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,610
Hmm, pretty clever system.

15
00:02:34,390 --> 00:02:35,630
What are you talking about?

16
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:38,370
About how dungeons are made, isn't it obvious?

17
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:42,690
It was a while ago, but I studied it back when I was in school.

18
00:02:43,490 --> 00:02:45,410
It's a lot more complex than you'd think.

19
00:02:45,410 --> 00:02:49,470
Hey, isn't that Marcelle?

20
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:51,590
You know, from the graduate course?

21
00:02:51,910 --> 00:02:54,130
She was the school's very first genius.

22
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:58,570
Yeah, I heard she was the teacher's assistant the first day.

23
00:02:58,770 --> 00:03:01,950
And I heard that they've decided she's going to be a court magician.

24
00:03:02,230 --> 00:03:03,670
Really? That's amazing!

25
00:03:04,050 --> 00:03:04,310
Hmm.

26
00:03:05,450 --> 00:03:08,730
Actually, I wasn't assisting the teacher until the fifth day of school.

27
00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:11,710
And the court magician thing is because my mom was one, too.

28
00:03:11,710 --> 00:03:18,210
By the way, I kind of pestered the teacher to let me join class today.

29
00:03:18,830 --> 00:03:20,790
So hi. Glad to be here.

30
00:03:21,890 --> 00:03:23,570
Uh, hey!

31
00:03:25,090 --> 00:03:28,290
Today we're going to experiment with spirit cultivation.

32
00:03:29,090 --> 00:03:31,850
I want each of you to grab a jar and head outside.

33
00:03:33,650 --> 00:03:35,950
Using wooden discs with a hole in them,

34
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:40,850
place a disc and then a layer of soil on top and begin alternating.

35
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:44,210
Create a barrier over it,

36
00:03:44,590 --> 00:03:47,210
and then fill the jar with mana.

37
00:03:48,350 --> 00:03:50,310
Release some spirits inside.

38
00:03:52,310 --> 00:03:55,830
The microscopic spirits will live off the mana in the vessel.

39
00:03:56,910 --> 00:03:59,950
They'll die if the mana is too dense or too thin.

40
00:04:00,610 --> 00:04:03,510
Raising spirits is the foundation for summoning magic.

41
00:04:04,030 --> 00:04:05,710
The vessel we keep them in is called a dungeonium

42
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:09,390
because it looks similar to the structure of a monster-ridden dungeon.

43
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:13,210
When you finish, place it in the dark room.

44
00:04:13,650 --> 00:04:15,990
We'll see how they're doing in a week's time.

45
00:04:17,130 --> 00:04:17,690
Wow!

46
00:04:18,230 --> 00:04:20,390
Marcel, your barrier's so pretty!

47
00:04:20,770 --> 00:04:22,750
I can't believe this was your first time!

48
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:25,730
Although, why the interest in summoning magic?

49
00:04:26,130 --> 00:04:26,350
Huh?

50
00:04:26,350 --> 00:04:28,430
It's not like it's your specialty.

51
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:32,470
I've been researching things to learn how to build a safe dungeon.

52
00:04:32,990 --> 00:04:35,230
I'm on magic ingredients now.

53
00:04:36,190 --> 00:04:40,650
For example, ingredients like mandrakes are pretty dangerous to harvest.

54
00:04:42,330 --> 00:04:47,410
However, if we could create a safe dungeon that's inhabited by monsters that are useful,

55
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:50,090
then it would greatly contribute to society!

56
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:51,450
Whoa!

57
00:04:51,450 --> 00:04:53,810
That sounds amazing!

58
00:04:54,130 --> 00:04:55,590
Look at Marcel's barrier!

59
00:04:55,930 --> 00:04:57,210
It's so enchanting!

60
00:04:57,490 --> 00:04:58,690
Hey, can I see too?

61
00:04:58,870 --> 00:05:00,150
Make some room for me!

62
00:05:00,770 --> 00:05:01,410
Careful!

63
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:05,770
Are you hurt?

64
00:05:06,350 --> 00:05:07,910
Oh, no, I'm okay.

65
00:05:11,270 --> 00:05:14,050
There are some impurities mixed in the soil.

66
00:05:14,690 --> 00:05:17,510
And the mana's thin because the barrier is full of holes.

67
00:05:18,430 --> 00:05:21,410
In that state, the spirits inside won't live long.

68
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:23,930
You didn't get dirt on your clothes, did you?

69
00:05:24,290 --> 00:05:24,630
Huh?

70
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:30,130
That girl, she's always covered in dirt and ditches claths so people think she's weird.

71
00:05:31,550 --> 00:05:32,110
Huh.

72
00:05:35,550 --> 00:05:39,050
Now then, when everyone has their jars in front of them,

73
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:42,270
we'll see how your spirits have developed over the past week.

74
00:05:42,590 --> 00:05:43,590
Are you kidding?

75
00:05:43,950 --> 00:05:45,150
Mine are all dead!

76
00:05:45,350 --> 00:05:46,890
Wow, mine somehow survived!

77
00:05:46,890 --> 00:05:48,670
Is this a new type of spirit?

78
00:05:48,850 --> 00:05:49,850
You mean the mold?

79
00:05:50,630 --> 00:05:54,810
If a good number of them survived, the fire will be large.

80
00:05:57,390 --> 00:06:00,190
Looks like your spirits are being maintained nicely.

81
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:01,690
Excellent work, Marcel.

82
00:06:01,690 --> 00:06:11,130
What's happening to my jar?

83
00:06:11,770 --> 00:06:13,850
That's quite a lot of spirits there.

84
00:06:14,350 --> 00:06:15,350
What do I do?

85
00:06:15,350 --> 00:06:18,330
Don't worry, I'll handle it.

86
00:06:18,830 --> 00:06:19,750
Please tell me!

87
00:06:19,970 --> 00:06:20,810
How'd you do that?

88
00:06:20,850 --> 00:06:21,710
I need to know!

89
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:27,030
Well, you see, I know a place pretty close by that has a lot of spirits.

90
00:06:27,550 --> 00:06:30,830
I thought my dungeonium would work better if I used soil from there.

91
00:06:31,230 --> 00:06:32,870
There's a place like that nearby?

92
00:06:33,430 --> 00:06:34,450
Can you tell me where?

93
00:06:35,410 --> 00:06:37,230
Oh, it's the...

94
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:39,470
This is the same amount as in a real dungeon.

95
00:06:39,810 --> 00:06:41,750
This'll be a fine sample indeed.

96
00:06:45,690 --> 00:06:47,610
I got it from a real dungeon.

97
00:06:51,190 --> 00:06:53,010
We can get outside from here!

98
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:56,330
This was here the whole time?

99
00:07:18,950 --> 00:07:22,050
So are you always doing stuff like this?

100
00:07:22,050 --> 00:07:22,890
Yep.

101
00:07:25,830 --> 00:07:27,650
That's why people think she's weird.

102
00:07:37,970 --> 00:07:38,930
It's a bug!

103
00:07:40,090 --> 00:07:41,250
Delicious fruit!

104
00:07:43,390 --> 00:07:46,130
You can't just pick up and eat random crap you find!

105
00:07:46,250 --> 00:07:47,130
You've got to be careful!

106
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:48,810
What if those things poisoned you?

107
00:07:49,370 --> 00:07:51,990
Oh, but I actually know what these things are.

108
00:07:52,470 --> 00:07:54,830
Grasshoppers and raspberries aren't poisonous.

109
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:02,730
So it really is a dungeon.

110
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:04,370
This is amazing.

111
00:08:06,070 --> 00:08:09,990
The mana here is stagnant and the air is stale.

112
00:08:10,510 --> 00:08:12,430
Seems like it's a natural cave.

113
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:15,410
Wait, don't go in there!

114
00:08:21,210 --> 00:08:22,210
Oh, don't worry.

115
00:08:22,850 --> 00:08:24,010
I come here often.

116
00:08:24,610 --> 00:08:26,670
Stay on dry ground and it's perfectly safe.

117
00:08:26,670 --> 00:08:31,610
uh,

118
00:08:31,690 --> 00:08:35,610
hmm, hmm, hmm, hmm.

119
00:08:42,410 --> 00:08:43,090
Hmm.

120
00:08:44,550 --> 00:08:45,330
Hmm.

121
00:08:45,330 --> 00:08:46,450
Hmm.

122
00:08:46,450 --> 00:08:47,130
Hmm.

123
00:08:47,450 --> 00:08:47,870
Hmm.

124
00:08:48,790 --> 00:08:48,930
Mostly.

125
00:08:48,930 --> 00:08:52,470
The inside of the dungeon really is swarming with spirits, huh?

126
00:08:54,990 --> 00:08:58,290
I took some dirt and water from here and added it to my jar.

127
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:01,430
That explains it.

128
00:09:01,950 --> 00:09:03,890
So what do you come to this place to do?

129
00:09:05,770 --> 00:09:08,350
I usually write letters or do some reading.

130
00:09:09,350 --> 00:09:12,010
Well, they weren't wrong about her ditching class.

131
00:09:15,370 --> 00:09:18,350
Anyway, there's nothing dangerous yet.

132
00:09:19,370 --> 00:09:20,050
Wait.

133
00:09:20,710 --> 00:09:24,170
If we tilt this dirt and planted some mandrakes,

134
00:09:24,390 --> 00:09:26,950
I think we could safely utilize the dungeon's mana.

135
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:31,890
There's even a water source close by, so it's definitely possible.

136
00:09:35,210 --> 00:09:37,750
Oh, crap! This is bad!

137
00:09:38,310 --> 00:09:40,770
Just stand back! I'll get rid of this slime monster!

138
00:09:40,770 --> 00:09:41,170
Wait!

139
00:09:41,530 --> 00:09:47,370
What do you think you're doing?

140
00:09:48,930 --> 00:09:52,850
It won't come into the sunlight. You don't have to worry, I promise!

141
00:09:56,950 --> 00:10:00,850
Slimes are actually able to break down bat droppings and then turn them into mana.

142
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:06,310
If the slimes weren't here to do that, the dungeon would die.

143
00:10:09,530 --> 00:10:10,370
Bats, huh?

144
00:10:11,570 --> 00:10:12,470
Take this.

145
00:10:12,470 --> 00:10:26,390
It's good.

146
00:10:26,390 --> 00:10:31,370
If they're this good, I bet the animals around here probably eat them.

147
00:10:32,970 --> 00:10:36,290
I wonder what kinds of things the bats up there eat.

148
00:10:37,430 --> 00:10:39,830
And what season do these raspberries grow in?

149
00:10:40,270 --> 00:10:41,890
What kind of animals eat them?

150
00:10:41,890 --> 00:10:46,210
I can't make a dungeon without knowing things like that.

151
00:10:50,810 --> 00:10:53,290
I still have so much left to learn.

152
00:10:53,290 --> 00:10:59,810
Thanks so much for bringing me here.

153
00:11:01,010 --> 00:11:05,770
The truth is, I thought if I'd just studied spells and magic, that was all I'd need to know.

154
00:11:06,290 --> 00:11:07,570
But that's not true.

155
00:11:07,570 --> 00:11:13,550
Oh, I haven't introduced myself.

156
00:11:14,230 --> 00:11:15,070
My name's Valen.

157
00:11:15,530 --> 00:11:17,290
Would you mind telling me your name?

158
00:11:19,850 --> 00:11:26,350
My name is Marcel.

159
00:11:27,490 --> 00:11:30,310
Valen, what do you say to becoming friends?

160
00:11:30,310 --> 00:11:36,370
The part about you being the school's first genius has to be a lie, right?

161
00:11:36,670 --> 00:11:38,070
Why would you think it's a lie?

162
00:11:38,170 --> 00:11:40,450
I'll have you know that I was an honor student.

163
00:11:42,290 --> 00:11:45,550
Anyway, this whole dungeon's pretty unbelievable.

164
00:11:46,470 --> 00:11:51,270
There are layers of calculations going on and tons of mana being circulated.

165
00:11:51,270 --> 00:11:57,110
If the mad mage is really out there somewhere, they're not just your average magic user.

166
00:11:57,110 --> 00:12:01,710
With that said, it's probably best if you stop living here, Senshi.

167
00:12:02,390 --> 00:12:03,730
Mind your own business.

168
00:12:04,530 --> 00:12:05,010
Seriously!

169
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:06,730
You hate magic, right?

170
00:12:06,850 --> 00:12:09,410
Well, the dungeon itself is entirely made out of it!

171
00:12:10,390 --> 00:12:11,430
Can't hear ya.

172
00:12:13,110 --> 00:12:14,090
I see.

173
00:12:14,810 --> 00:12:16,630
So Valen was talking about you.

174
00:12:17,850 --> 00:12:21,410
When she enrolled into magic school, she would send me update letters.

175
00:12:22,010 --> 00:12:25,350
I could tell that she was anxious there at first, but...

176
00:12:25,350 --> 00:12:27,850
One day, she wrote about how she made a new friend.

177
00:12:28,510 --> 00:12:30,090
And she sounded a lot happier.

178
00:12:33,030 --> 00:12:34,810
She always praised you, Marcel.

179
00:12:36,110 --> 00:12:37,590
She thought you were awesome.

180
00:12:43,590 --> 00:12:45,390
Valen praised you too, Laios.

181
00:12:45,610 --> 00:12:47,010
She really looked up to you.

182
00:12:47,010 --> 00:12:49,550
Is that so?

183
00:12:51,790 --> 00:12:53,110
What's so great about him?

184
00:12:53,290 --> 00:12:55,730
He's got the best dog impression I've ever heard!

185
00:12:56,890 --> 00:13:00,410
Maybe that's something I should keep between me and Valen for now.

186
00:13:01,410 --> 00:13:05,130
Well, let's get our butts in gear and go save Valen!

187
00:13:06,870 --> 00:13:08,330
Come on, you tin can!

188
00:13:08,450 --> 00:13:10,610
You're awake, so get up so we can get going!

189
00:13:10,610 --> 00:13:14,170
We're currently here.

190
00:13:14,890 --> 00:13:18,310
The orcs we talked to mentioned the red dragon had appeared right here.

191
00:13:18,710 --> 00:13:20,270
It'll take two days to get there.

192
00:13:21,150 --> 00:13:26,210
It's probably not where we left it, but dragons also aren't really the type to wander far.

193
00:13:26,770 --> 00:13:28,970
We should only make camp two more times.

194
00:13:29,710 --> 00:13:33,450
First at the halfway mark, and lastly right before the dragon.

195
00:13:34,250 --> 00:13:36,450
We'll wake up Laios when the candle burns out.

196
00:13:37,230 --> 00:13:38,230
Do what you need now.

197
00:13:38,990 --> 00:13:40,570
We won't rest again for a while.

198
00:13:43,530 --> 00:13:44,730
I'd like to wash up.

199
00:13:46,550 --> 00:13:46,990
Seriously?

200
00:13:47,610 --> 00:13:49,010
I can do it in the corner.

201
00:13:50,710 --> 00:13:51,990
Just be quick about it.

202
00:13:56,550 --> 00:13:58,310
We'll be outside if you need us.

203
00:13:59,450 --> 00:14:00,730
It's fine if you stay.

204
00:14:00,970 --> 00:14:01,970
I'm not getting naked.

205
00:14:03,450 --> 00:14:04,690
Uh, okay.

206
00:14:06,850 --> 00:14:09,290
Man, I sure do make them worry.

207
00:14:10,570 --> 00:14:13,330
Wonder if I should have studied illusion magic too.

208
00:14:14,370 --> 00:14:16,050
No, that's not the problem.

209
00:14:16,670 --> 00:14:19,010
It's because I'm the only girl in the party now.

210
00:14:20,430 --> 00:14:22,210
We'll be parting ways here.

211
00:14:22,730 --> 00:14:23,830
Are you serious?

212
00:14:24,270 --> 00:14:25,910
Does it really have to be now?

213
00:14:26,190 --> 00:14:29,110
I mean, we still don't know where Valen is after all.

214
00:14:29,110 --> 00:14:33,990
Sorry, but we have our own livelihoods to worry about.

215
00:14:35,670 --> 00:14:38,630
Just remembering that moment makes me mad.

216
00:14:39,070 --> 00:14:40,850
I thought that we were all friends.

217
00:14:45,470 --> 00:14:46,770
Wake up, Laios.

218
00:14:47,250 --> 00:14:48,410
Hey, come on.

219
00:14:48,710 --> 00:14:49,510
Time to get moving.

220
00:14:49,510 --> 00:14:52,690
There we go.

221
00:14:54,330 --> 00:14:55,830
Guess I boiled too much.

222
00:14:55,830 --> 00:14:56,290
She'll be OK.

223
00:14:56,290 --> 00:15:26,270
Let's go.

224
00:15:26,290 --> 00:15:31,790
What's wrong?

225
00:15:34,510 --> 00:15:35,470
What?

226
00:15:43,350 --> 00:15:44,910
My water walking?

227
00:15:45,410 --> 00:15:46,450
The water's moving.

228
00:15:46,970 --> 00:15:49,270
Weapons won't work. We need fire.

229
00:15:49,890 --> 00:15:50,310
Fire?

230
00:15:52,530 --> 00:15:53,830
I'll start one.

231
00:15:53,830 --> 00:15:56,670
Hey, Marcel! Hold on a bit longer!

232
00:15:57,230 --> 00:15:58,790
Easy for you to say.

233
00:15:59,870 --> 00:16:01,550
Please let this hit it.

234
00:16:01,550 --> 00:16:03,550
Come on.

235
00:16:21,670 --> 00:16:22,230
Marcel!

236
00:16:22,890 --> 00:16:24,450
What are you waiting for? Go!

237
00:16:25,270 --> 00:16:26,790
All of you, stay there!

238
00:16:26,950 --> 00:16:29,450
My water walking spell is wearing off, so...

239
00:16:34,010 --> 00:16:37,070
Marcel!

240
00:16:37,750 --> 00:16:38,470
Get up!

241
00:16:38,890 --> 00:16:39,450
Keep moving!

242
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:50,610
I won't be able to run now.

243
00:16:50,610 --> 00:17:00,050
Where is it hiding?

244
00:17:08,050 --> 00:17:13,930
I can't watch! Come on, Senshi! Hurry up!

245
00:17:13,930 --> 00:17:15,770
I'm growing as fast as I can!

246
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:16,830
This is bad.

247
00:17:18,270 --> 00:17:22,270
I don't have much mana left.

248
00:17:22,770 --> 00:17:24,730
I've got to get it in the next shot.

249
00:17:30,770 --> 00:17:31,290
Where?

250
00:17:32,770 --> 00:17:33,910
Where is it?

251
00:17:33,910 --> 00:17:36,430
There must be some kind of clue.

252
00:17:38,230 --> 00:17:38,750
There!

253
00:17:40,370 --> 00:17:41,670
It has my blood!

254
00:17:42,910 --> 00:17:44,010
It's so fast.

255
00:17:51,810 --> 00:17:52,850
Just hold on!

256
00:17:52,850 --> 00:18:10,790
I don't talk to you!

257
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:11,770
Hey, guys?

258
00:18:13,190 --> 00:18:14,510
What now?

259
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:19,250
All right, here's the plan.

260
00:18:22,330 --> 00:18:24,270
Let's get out of here!

261
00:18:26,590 --> 00:18:32,030
How are you holding up, Marcel?

262
00:18:33,310 --> 00:18:36,950
I stopped the bleeding, but I'm low on blood and mana.

263
00:18:37,830 --> 00:18:39,030
So I'm spent.

264
00:18:40,210 --> 00:18:40,810
Sorry.

265
00:18:41,550 --> 00:18:42,170
It's fine.

266
00:18:42,730 --> 00:18:43,750
Just take it easy.

267
00:18:45,010 --> 00:18:50,030
I really should have paid more attention when Fallon was teaching me healing magic.

268
00:18:51,190 --> 00:18:52,530
Hey, Laios?

269
00:18:53,150 --> 00:18:55,770
What are we gonna do now?

270
00:18:56,270 --> 00:18:59,730
There's no way we can take a monolith magic user further into the dungeon.

271
00:19:00,210 --> 00:19:03,610
And we can't continue on without the help of her water walking spell.

272
00:19:03,970 --> 00:19:05,990
Let's wait for other adventurers to pass by.

273
00:19:06,830 --> 00:19:09,110
If we're lucky, one of them will be a healer.

274
00:19:09,590 --> 00:19:13,830
There's no way that someone who's willing to help others would conveniently pass by here.

275
00:19:13,830 --> 00:19:16,390
Besides, we don't have anything we can trade.

276
00:19:17,090 --> 00:19:19,750
Yeah, I think the only thing we have is kelpie meat.

277
00:19:20,010 --> 00:19:21,550
Let's hope the person is starving.

278
00:19:22,510 --> 00:19:24,890
It's a rare nutrient source in a dungeon.

279
00:19:24,890 --> 00:19:28,150
Who cares about nutrition right now?

280
00:19:29,470 --> 00:19:33,390
Actually, did you happen to grab its liver too, Senshi?

281
00:19:33,850 --> 00:19:34,770
Of course I did.

282
00:19:35,330 --> 00:19:37,570
Livers are too rich in iron to leave behind.

283
00:19:38,310 --> 00:19:38,590
Hmm?

284
00:19:39,770 --> 00:19:40,070
Huh?

285
00:19:40,070 --> 00:19:41,910
I knew it.

286
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:44,070
That means...

287
00:19:45,450 --> 00:19:47,170
It's grilling time!

288
00:19:53,570 --> 00:20:03,610
Mane, neck, liver, ribs, tail, thigh, loin, and veggies.

289
00:20:03,610 --> 00:20:09,550
Marcelle?

290
00:20:10,550 --> 00:20:11,230
Marcelle?

291
00:20:13,490 --> 00:20:14,790
You good to sit up?

292
00:20:15,650 --> 00:20:17,450
We made something nice for you.

293
00:20:17,450 --> 00:20:17,490
Yeah?

294
00:20:17,490 --> 00:20:18,050
Mm-hmm.

295
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:35,010
Thigh.

296
00:20:35,830 --> 00:20:36,790
Where's the liver?

297
00:20:37,570 --> 00:20:40,190
You gotta make sure organs get cooked all the way.

298
00:20:40,190 --> 00:20:46,910
Forgive me, Marcelle, but I'm digging in.

299
00:20:47,950 --> 00:20:48,250
Ow!

300
00:20:50,410 --> 00:20:51,590
That's pretty good.

301
00:20:52,130 --> 00:20:52,690
Yeah.

302
00:20:52,990 --> 00:20:54,870
It's a little chewy, but I like it.

303
00:20:55,330 --> 00:20:58,730
Does it taste more like a horse or a marine animal?

304
00:20:59,530 --> 00:21:02,190
I haven't eaten either, so I can't really compare it.

305
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:04,190
Ribs.

306
00:21:04,190 --> 00:21:06,530
It tastes sweet, doesn't it?

307
00:21:06,790 --> 00:21:08,190
Yeah, and so soft.

308
00:21:08,890 --> 00:21:10,350
Marcelle, the liver's ready now.

309
00:21:12,190 --> 00:21:12,750
Tenderloin.

310
00:21:13,810 --> 00:21:15,790
It's like it's melting in my mouth.

311
00:21:16,070 --> 00:21:17,410
I really like this one.

312
00:21:18,070 --> 00:21:19,230
Here's some liver, Marcelle.

313
00:21:20,330 --> 00:21:20,890
Tail.

314
00:21:22,230 --> 00:21:22,790
Yummy.

315
00:21:23,310 --> 00:21:25,410
An interesting flavor on this one.

316
00:21:26,210 --> 00:21:26,890
Here, Marcelle.

317
00:21:27,710 --> 00:21:29,450
Have more liver, Marcelle.

318
00:21:30,030 --> 00:21:31,410
How is it, Marcelle?

319
00:21:31,690 --> 00:21:33,030
Eat some more, Marcelle.

320
00:21:33,030 --> 00:21:34,790
You like it, Marcelle?

321
00:21:39,890 --> 00:21:40,410
Please.

322
00:21:42,670 --> 00:21:44,790
Please give me the other parts, too!

323
00:21:49,930 --> 00:21:51,950
Well, it looks like she's starting to recover.

324
00:21:52,450 --> 00:21:53,570
Liver's amazing.

325
00:21:54,790 --> 00:21:57,350
That aside, what do we do about her low mana?

326
00:21:57,850 --> 00:22:00,470
Yeah, if only there was a meat that could help restore it.

327
00:22:00,470 --> 00:22:03,030
Why'd you stuff the basilisk with monoherbs?

328
00:22:03,230 --> 00:22:04,970
I still stand by my choice.

329
00:22:10,810 --> 00:22:12,130
Do you smell that?

330
00:22:13,090 --> 00:22:14,550
It's coming from below.

331
00:22:14,890 --> 00:22:16,010
What is that?

332
00:22:16,510 --> 00:22:18,690
I think it's grilled meat.

333
00:22:19,570 --> 00:22:21,210
Someone below must be cooking it.

334
00:22:21,210 --> 00:22:26,270
Jeez, you gotta be kidding me.

335
00:22:27,590 --> 00:22:29,810
What kind of moron would be grilling meat in here?

